    say NO WORK for a model killed before it could start - because it is
    
    The two no-work paths logged differently: one said 'it did NO WORK', the other said 'it did NOT finish'. The second is true about the work it left and wrong about the outcome - a model killed before it could start did no work, and the chain treats it as no work, so the log should say so.

