commit 44a3e1003b4ee318ecb1bf08715edd3764dd6269
Author: authorss81 <authorss81@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 20 13:20:28 2026 +0530

    fix: the tree rule must not judge a model that never ran
    
    My own change broke the dead-model-chain path. The tree rule fired on any model
    that left the tree untouched - including a model that never got to try, because
    of a rate limit, a revoked free tier, or a dead model id. A dead chain then
    advanced, hit the two-in-a-row limit, and BLOCKED the phase, where it used to
    defer without consuming an attempt. Four smoke checks caught it: the chain now
    exits 3 where 42 was expected.
    
    The tree only answers the question for a model that RAN: exit 0 with real
    output, and the tree byte-for-byte unchanged. That is exactly the shape of
    phase-062's fix round 3 - it read for ten minutes, narrated at length, exited 0,
    and changed nothing.
    
    A model that never ran is a different thing, and it keeps its old handling: the
    chain advances, and a wholly dead chain defers.
    
    The wording in the smoke check follows the log line.

